ENTRY            30066   20191211   20200416   20200416       3195
SUBENT        30066001   20191211   20200416   20200416       3195
BIB                 11         32
TITLE      Investigation of the cross-section of neutron
            reactions in the nucleus Rh103
AUTHOR     (J.Csikai, J.Bacso, A.Daroczy)
INSTITUTE  (3HUNDEB)
REFERENCE  (J,NP,41,316,1963)
           (J,AKS,5,(3-4),1,1963) details in Russian, tables
           (J,NP/A,95,229,1967) 103g+mRh data in table
INC-SOURCE (PHOTO)
           .Sb-Be source inside paraffin block with
            Cd-difference method for 0.032 eV neutrons.
           .Sb-Be source in scattering free environment for
            24 keV neutrons
           (D-C12) 116 keV neutrons
           (D-D) 2.49 MeV neutrons
           (D-T) 14.67 MeV neutrons
SAMPLE     Rh metal foil of 124 mg/cm2 thick
METHOD     (ACTIV)
DETECTOR   (GEMUC) Mica end-window GM counter, calibrated with
            UO2SO4 standard which geometry is identical to the
            foil geometry
           (LONGC) Long counter as flux monitor calibrated with
            a Po-Be neutron source.
ADD-RES    104Rh production cross section 1.69 b (for g.s.) and
            1.89 b (for total) at 24 keV assuming sig(ms)=0.2 b
            from V.Hummel et al., Phys.Rev.82(1951)67).
STATUS     (APRVD)  Approved by Peto (5/9/1972)
HISTORY    (19670713C) Compiled into DASTAR
           (19710106T) Converted to EXFOR, previously DASTAR-165.
           (20080305A) BIB section updated
           (20160209U) VS. DECAY-DATA correction in 005.
                       ERR-ANALYS 001->007
           (20191211A) On. Major revisions in 003-004.
ENDBIB              32
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           35
ENDENTRY             1
